---
title: A frame is a pure function
brief: The core rule stated as a formula, then the three things it gives you.
notes: Everything else in the system follows from this one line.
score:
  intro:
    - rise: rule
      at: 200
  steps:
    - name: what it gives you
      cues:
        - rise: [a, b, c]
          from: [0, 16]
          stagger: 140
---
<Header>One rule holds it <em>together</em></Header>
<Stack gap="28">
  <Card id="rule" tone="accent" label="The rule">
    <div class="mono" style="font-size:40px">render(document, slide, step, t) → pixels</div>
  </Card>
  <Grid cols="3">
    <Card id="a" title="Reproducible"><Text>Any moment of any animation is one call away.</Text></Card>
    <Card id="b" title="Checkable"><Text>Every step can be measured, not eyeballed.</Text></Card>
    <Card id="c" title="Exportable"><Text>PDF and images need no animation code at all.</Text></Card>
  </Grid>
</Stack>
